            {
              "row_id": "r1",
              "label": "B07 Operating driver — installed base and volume",
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "Management Language",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C35",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "S1 p.4: aircraft life “approximately 25 to 30 years”, platform production “20 to 30 years”, estimated product lifecycle “in excess of 50 years”. P.7 demand depends on “the breadth of our installed OEM base”, RPKs, fleet size/age, warranty and airline profitability; p.8 shipments “generally run ahead of aircraft delivery schedules.”",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C35",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Long exposure can extend replacement opportunity, while utilization and advance OEM shipment timing make orders cyclical → use lagged operating drivers and avoid assuming subscription-like visibility.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C35",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Lifecycle is an issuer estimate, not a contracted sales duration. No flight-hour sensitivity/backlog coverage metric established: measure = null.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C35",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                }
              ],
              "style": "row"
            },
            {
              "row_id": "r2",
              "label": "B08 Operating driver — pricing/cost structure",
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "Management Language",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C36",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "S1 pp.6,33 describes business-unit teams, productivity, lean costs and pricing products to reflect value. P.13 warns “Most of our contracts do not permit us to recover increases in raw material prices, taxes or labor costs.” P.9 certification can prevent efficient supplier replacement.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C36",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Pricing discretion in some niches does not remove fixed-price exposure or certification bottlenecks; volume absorption and cost inflation affect margins → stress price recovery and supply continuity separately.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C36",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Price/volume split, contractual escalation coverage and fixed/variable cost split: measure = null, Not disclosed. No automatic pass-through or proven pricing-power conclusion.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C36",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                }
              ],
              "style": "row"
            },
            {
              "row_id": "r3",
              "label": "B09 Operating driver — revenue recognition / contracts",
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "Documentary Fact",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C37",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "S1 p.120, Note 3: “A substantial portion of the Company’s revenue is recorded at a point in time basis”; limited over-time contracts use cost-to-cost input. P.13: “we do not generally have long-term contracts with most of our aftermarket customers” and OEM customers generally have no minimum-quantity commitment and may terminate on short notice.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C37",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Revenue requires delivery/control transfer or qualifying performance; future installed-base consumption is not assured backlog → forecast order realization, not annuity receipts.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C37",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Exact point-in-time share, guaranteed backlog, recurring contracted revenue and cancellation coverage: measure = null, Not disclosed.",
                  "prov": "cited",
                  "ref_id": "C37",
                  "gap_ref": null,
                  "unit_class": "text",
                  "state": "known"
                }
              ],
              "style": "row"
